Translate the 271 strings nothing could reach (1.15.0)

A systematic sweep, not the reported items one at a time: every
user-visible Persian literal that never passes through t(). It found 271,
of which 266 were not wrapped at all — no amount of translation would have
reached them.

Almost all were error and confirmation messages returned from server
actions as { error: '…' }. Wrapping 266 call sites would have been
invasive and easy to get wrong, so they are translated where they are
displayed instead: ~30 client components, one point each. The translator
falls back to the key, so an untranslated message still reads exactly as
it does today.

All 271 now have translations in the eight non-source languages.

Also fixed on the way:
- The settings tag table no longer prints the base name under the
  translated one. It was meant as a hint and read as "not translated".
- Meeting tabs and the conversation counter were passed as data, the same
  shape as `header` and `addLabel` before them.

